From 164e925f9285003d239583affd6d6ceef07e3c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:09:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: give thread organization a store of its own

Zeo's sidebar is about to gain a Pinned section, drag-reordered threads,
tags, cross-project lists and sub-threads linked to their parent (stories
for patches 0049-0055). Each needs to remember something per thread across
restarts. This patch is that memory, with no UI: story 031, 2026-10-09.

Why a domain of its own. sqlez migrations are positional per domain and a
changed step aborts startup ("Migration changed for {domain} at step
{index}"). A step appended to upstream's ThreadMetadataDb list would be
overtaken by upstream's next one and stop Zeo from starting. So
ThreadOrganizationDb is its own domain, beside upstream's in the same file,
with an append-only list -- the shape 0035's AgentTaskHistoryDb already
proved. Step 0 must never be edited once it ships; later stories append.

Schema (step 0):

  thread_organization(thread_id PK, pinned_position, manual_position,
                      manual_project_key, list_id, parent_thread_id,
                      fork_kind CHECK with_context|clean)
  thread_lists(id AUTOINCREMENT, name, name_key UNIQUE, position)
  thread_tags(thread_id, tag_key) PK both;  tags(tag_key PK, display)
  project_sort_mode(project_key PK, mode CHECK manual)

The project order itself is not here: upstream already persists it per
window (multi_workspace_state).

  thread_organization.rs adds ThreadOrganizationStore, a global entity that
  loads every row once (synchronously, retried on a busy read), answers
  from memory, and writes through one ordered background writer, one
  transaction per user action. Reads: organization, pinned, sort_mode,
  manual_position_in(thread, project), lists, threads_in_list, tags,
  all_tags, parent, children, sub_threads. Writes: pin/unpin/move_pinned,
  set_manual_order/set_sort_mode (per-project Recent or Manual),
  create/rename/move/delete_list, set_list, add/remove_tag, set_parent.

Rules decided with the requester: deleting a list keeps its threads, which
only lose the list; tags are case-insensitive (Unicode to_lowercase, never
SQL LOWER, which folds ASCII only) and display their first spelling; a
sub-thread outlives its parent with a dangling link; a draft (no session
yet) cannot be organized; an archived thread keeps everything. Limits: a
tag is 1-32 characters with no whitespace, '#' or ','; at most 20 per
thread; a list name is 1-64 characters, unique ignoring case.

ProjectKey is the JSON array [host, [sorted main-worktree paths]], host
null locally or ["ssh"|"wsl"|"docker", <the fields
same_remote_connection_identity compares>]: arrays, because an object's key
order depends on serde_json's preserve_order feature; JSON, because a
folder named "/a\n/b" must not collide with /a and /b.

Forward compatibility: only the columns this build owns are written
(INSERT .. ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE), the parent link by its own upsert. A row
holding a value this build does not recognize (a newer Zeo wrote it) is
skipped at load with a warning naming the thread, never overwritten, and
deleted only when its thread is.

Failure: the in-memory fallback (db::ALL_FILE_DB_FAILED) and a failed load
keep organization working for the session and warn once; a failed write
logs the operation and the thread or list ids -- never tag, list or project
text.

Upstream lines touched, three: `pub mod thread_organization;` and
`thread_organization::init(cx);` in agent_ui.rs, and
`crate::thread_organization::forget(thread_id, cx);` as the first line of
ThreadMetadataStore::delete, the funnel of every deletion path -- the shape
of the draft_prompt_store call there, placed at the top so 0036's hunk at the
end of delete keeps its context.
forget never reads ThreadMetadataStore (it runs inside its update) and
queues nothing for a thread with nothing stored: drafts are deleted all the
time. Every write that names a thread reads ThreadMetadataStore to refuse
drafts, so none may be called from inside its update, and threads are
unknown until its first load (reload_task).

Tests (72, crates/agent_ui/src/thread_organization/): migrations beside a
growing upstream domain and a reopen from step 0; normalization's hostile
halves (Rust/rust one tag, rust/rust-lang two, non-ASCII and final sigma);
project keys (folder order, hosts, separators, pinned stored form); the
store across restarts, refused writes changing nothing, the fallback
warning, failed writes logged without user text, skipped newer rows kept;
and deletion through the real ThreadMetadataStore::delete and delete_all.

Forward-ported to zeo 0.2.3 (upstream 089abd69) by story 032, 2026-10-09.
The new base asked for one change: test_helpers.rs imports
agent_client_protocol::schema::v2 as acp, since ThreadMetadata.session_id is
now an Option<v2::SessionId>. And one fix: delete_list cleared list_id only
on the rows it had loaded, so a row skipped at load (a newer Zeo wrote it)
kept naming the deleted list. Change::ClearList -- UPDATE thread_organization
SET list_id = NULL WHERE list_id = ? -- now runs in the same write before
DeleteList, the shape ClearManual already has, and leaves the skipped row's
other values as they were. Three more tests, in store_clear_list_tests.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
